      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SUPER TALON (6) comes here off a break of ten months. Worth noting he filled a minor placing when returning from a spell last time in work over 1100m at Mackay. Yet to win first up but generally runs well with two minor placings from three tries. Expect him to play a major role. JOEY D'OR (4) finished out of the money when tenth over 1350m at Ipswich three-and-a-half weeks ago. Finds a more suitable contest and can turn things around. CLAW MACHINE (1) failed to feature when seventh over 1015m at Toowoomba a week ago. Ideally placed and is sure to give this a mighty shake. STROMBOLI DELIGHT (8) has a moderate winning strike-rate but performed well last time at Bundaberg, finishing third and only 2.5 lengths from the winner at the end of 1380m. Well placed and should be about the money.",
